    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Logistic-SuSiE approximations: the 022 protocol on a Gaussian and on a nested design\"\nsubtitle: \"CAVI-Q2 vs gIBSS-Q2 vs gIBSS-Laplace vs gIBSS-GO vs global-JJ vs local-JJ vs score (experiments 023 and 024, L=5, 200 reps)\"\nengine: jupyter\njupyter: python3\nexecute:\n  fig-dpi: 110\n---\n\n\nTwo analogs of the [022 full grid](full_grid.qmd). The protocol is 022's: $p = 256$,\n$b_0 = -2$, $L^* = 3$ equal causals at gap 8 (correlated) or 64 (independent), fit with\n$L = 5$, EB prior variance, the same seven arms in $\\mathcal{Q}_2$, 200 replicates per cell.\ngIBSS-GO (Gaussian offset) is gIBSS-Q2 with each leave-one-out offset replaced by a Gaussian\nsurrogate, moment-matched to the other components, and integrated over (5-component\nprobit-mixture approximation to the logistic, error under $10^{-6}$); it runs at $L = 5$ only.\nOnly the design and its sweep change.\n\n- **023, Gaussian.** AR(1) Gaussian columns, $n = 500$, adjacent $\\rho = 0.9$ (causal-causal\n  latent correlation $0.9^8 = 0.43$ at gap 8, $\\approx 0$ at gap 64). Every column is dense and\n  $N(0, 1)$, so there is no set-size axis; the sweep is the signal $T = E[\\text{LRT}]$ per\n  causal in $\\{4, 8, 12, 16, 20, 24\\}$, with one $\\beta$ per $T$. The dense control for 022's\n  sparse-set findings.\n- **024, nested.** `binary_attrition_X`: Markov roots (phi 0.8, half the rows) expanded into 32\n  blocks of 8 nested sets, each step keeping 55% of the parent's members, so one matrix holds\n  sets from 500 members down to 8. $n = 1000$. The sweep is the causals' depth $d \\in 0..7$,\n  i.e. their expected size $500 \\cdot 0.55^d$ (022's $m$), with $\\beta$ per $(d, T)$ and\n  $T \\in \\{8, 16\\}$. Causals sit at the same depth in blocks gap/8 apart; their decoys are\n  their own ancestors and descendants at other sizes.\n\nAll CS metrics are over **declared** CSs (component $\\log \\text{BF} \\ge 2$), as in 022.\n\n::: {#status .cell execution_count=2}\n- `023-laplace-gaussian`: 12 signal cells x 7 arms, 200-200 reps per cell; 200 null reps per arm.\n- `024-laplace-nested`: 32 signal cells x 7 arms, 200-200 reps per cell; 200 null reps per arm.\n:::\n\n\n# 023: Gaussian design, signal axis {#sec-gauss}\n\n## Headline: per gap, pooled over T {#sec-gauss-pooled}\n\n::: {#tab-gauss-pooled .cell execution_count=3}\nCAVI-Q2 in absolute terms; every other arm as **arm minus CAVI-Q2** on the same replicates. *coverage*: fraction of declared CSs containing a causal. *size*: median declared-CS size with its interquartile range. *power*: mean over reps of the fraction of the 3 causals captured by a declared CS. *CS/fit*: declared CSs per fit. 95% CIs resample replicates, jointly for both arms of a difference. One row per T x gap cell (there is no size axis to pool over).\n\n| T | gap | arm | coverage [95% CI] | size (IQR) | power [95% CI] | CS/fit |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 4 | 8 | CAVI-Q2 | 0.842 [0.757, 0.920] | 9 (5-14) | 0.172 [0.135, 0.210] | 0.38 |\n| 4 | 8 | gIBSS-GO | -0.009 [-0.021, -0.001] | 7 (5-14) | -0.013 [-0.030, +0.000] | 0.36 |\n| 4 | 8 | gIBSS-Q2 | -0.004 [-0.027, +0.026] | 8 (5-14) | -0.017 [-0.040, +0.005] | 0.34 |\n| 4 | 8 | gIBSS-Laplace | -0.004 [-0.027, +0.026] | 8 (5-13) | -0.018 [-0.040, +0.003] | 0.34 |\n| 4 | 8 | local-JJ | -0.024 [-0.048, -0.008] | 7 (4-12) | -0.035 [-0.062, -0.010] | 0.33 |\n| 4 | 8 | global-JJ | -0.175 [-0.277, -0.075] | 2 (2-4) | -0.117 [-0.152, -0.083] | 0.24 |\n| 4 | 8 | score | +0.019 [-0.022, +0.071] | 8 (5-14) | -0.015 [-0.045, +0.012] | 0.33 |\n| 4 | 64 | CAVI-Q2 | 0.750 [0.500, 1.000] | 7 (4-12) | 0.015 [0.007, 0.025] | 0.06 |\n| 4 | 64 | gIBSS-GO | +0.000 [+0.000, +0.000] | 7 (4-13) | +0.002 [+0.000, +0.005] | 0.06 |\n| 4 | 64 | gIBSS-Q2 | -0.050 [-0.167, +0.000] | 7 (4-9) | -0.002 [-0.007, +0.003] | 0.05 |\n| 4 | 64 | gIBSS-Laplace | -0.050 [-0.167, +0.000] | 7 (4-9) | -0.002 [-0.007, +0.003] | 0.05 |\n| 4 | 64 | local-JJ | -0.050 [-0.167, +0.000] | 7 (4-9) | -0.003 [-0.00